From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:16:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: clear PSE TDMA shared-buffer disable only with SOE

airoha_fe_init() clears PSE_TDMA_SHARE_BUF_DIS in REG_PSE_FC_CFG on
every board. The step mirrors the vendor EN7581 FE init, which lets the
flow control of the TDMA port, PSE port 7 (FE_PSE_PORT_CDM4), use the
PSE shared buffer. The SOE datapath was brought up with the bit cleared,
since SOE submissions are queued on PSE port 7 OQ8/OQ9 ahead of the SOE
hop.

PSE port 7 also carries the PPE-bound Wi-Fi traffic towards the NPU.
Without the SOE the driver never wrote this register and the bit stays
set, so the unconditional clear changes the PSE buffering of the Wi-Fi
offload path on boards whose SOE node is disabled or absent, without
anything on those boards needing it.

Clear the bit only when eth->soe_present is set, so the SOE keeps the
configuration it was brought up with. Without the SOE, REG_PSE_FC_CFG
is not written at all and the PSE setup matches the driver without SOE
support.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -874,7 +874,9 @@ static int airoha_fe_init(struct airoha_
 	/* SOE/TDMA output depends on PSE shared-buffer flow control instead
 	 * of leaving port-local sharing disabled.
 	 */
-	airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_PSE_FC_CFG, PSE_TDMA_SHARE_BUF_DIS_MASK);
+	if (eth->soe_present)
+		airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_PSE_FC_CFG,
+				PSE_TDMA_SHARE_BUF_DIS_MASK);
 
 	airoha_fe_vip_setup(eth);
 	airoha_fe_pse_ports_init(eth);
